  "text": "Emergency Vet in Wilmington, NC | Eastern Carolina Veterinary Medical Center\nSkip to Primary Content\nContact Us\nContact Us\nMap\n50 Greenville Ave,\nWilmington,\nNC,\n28403\nCall\n(910) 790-1070\nEmergency Care\nEmergency Care\nPhone:\n(910) 790-1070\nAddress:\n50 Greenville Ave,\nWilmington,\nNC,\n28403\nCareers\nDonate Today\nAbout Us\nAbout Us\nOur Team\nJoin Our Team\nWhat is a Specialist?\nRelocation Updates\nServices\nView all Services\nEmergency Care\nCritical Care\nGrief Counseling\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine & Rehabilitation\nSurgery\nTotal Hip Replacement (THR)\nPet Owners\nFor Pet Owners\nPayment Policy\nPrescription Refill Request\nSocial Work\nFor Veterinarians\nFor Veterinarians\nReferral Portal\nSubscribe to Our Newsletter\nEmergency Care\nContact Us\nExplore our Services\nLearn More\nIf you have a pet emergency, we're here 24/7.\nContact Us\nExplore our Services\nLearn More\nIf you have a pet emergency, we're here 24/7.\nContact Us\nExplore our Services\nLearn More\nWelcome to Eastern Carolina Veterinary Medical Center\nPreviously known as Eastern Carolina Veterinary Referral\nSERVING WILMINGTON, LELAND, WRIGHTSVILLE BEACH, CAROLINA BEACH, AND HAMPSTEAD, NC\nOur Mission\nOur mission is to provide premium-quality, state-of-the-art veterinary emergency and specialty care to our small animal patients and their owners in Wilmington, Leland, Wrightsville Beach, and the surrounding areas while meeting the needs of consulting veterinarians as an extension of their healthcare team.\nOur Team\nGive Us A Call\nPhone:\n(910) 790-1070\nFax:\n(910) 790-9669\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\nEmergency care is available 24/7. Specialty services are available by appointment.\nReviews & Client Testimonials\nOur 9 year old American Bulldog has to have TPLO surgery as well as a little work on her meniscus. The entire staff was helpful, thorough, and compassionate. The surgeon took as long as was needed to answer questions and make sure we were comfortable with the procedure. Still a ways to go with the recovery, but very pleased with their care so far.\nMitchell S.\nWe recently brought our cat in to the emergency hospital. From the very first contact, the staff was kind and reassuring. All of the staff treated us with so much compassion. They gave us great tools and instructions and updates and were upfront about the costs. We are not out of the woods yet, but so hopeful to bring our sweet boy home thanks to the incredible care he’s receiving. Thank you for your vigilant care of our sweet cat, Flynn. He’s the best cat in the world!\nRebecca G.\nOur dog Sammy was in labor and she was having difficulty delivering her first puppy. Dr Natalie Orner and the rest of the ECVMC team stepped right in and tried to help her deliver without surgery.  Ultimately, she needed a C-Section. We have 3 beautiful puppies and Sammy is doing great.  They are professional and kind and I'm so glad they were there for us.\nLucy L.\nEastern Carolina Veterinary Medical Center\n50 Greenville Ave\nWilmington\n,\nNC\n28403\nT:\n(910) 790-1070\nF:\n(910) 790-9669\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\nEmergency care is available 24/7. Specialty services are available by appointment.\nContact Us\nOur Team\nServices\nFor Veterinarians\nCareers\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nSMS PRIVACY POLICY\nAccessibility\nCookie Preferences\nDo Not Sell or Share My Information\n©\nCopyright\n2026",
